35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Guys, the account is thinner than it looks! Most of our costs are fixed, and some people are really struggling to pay the lump sum on time.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,I've noticed a worrying trend. People are hesitating to come out. It seems that any perceived cost per visit creates a psychological barrier.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's worse than I thought. A tiny group is doing all the work and attending everything, while others pay the same and never show up. It's unfair.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The treasurer's logs are alarming. Chasing small, individual payments takes six times as much work as a single annual collection. We cannot ignore this burden.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found something! A lot of people want to join mid-year, but they're scared of the big upfront cost. They want something more flexible!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,But we can't be too flexible if we can't cover the fixed costs! We need a guaranteed amount coming in early to keep the lights on.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, I understand the unfairness, but if we charge per-event to ""fix"" it, we might lose the members who are already on the fence.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"Why should the regulars carry the load? If we keep a flat fee, the people who never come are basically getting a free ride on our hard work.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, flexibility sounds good for the member, but it's a nightmare for the treasurer. We've already lost two people in three years because of the workload.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"But if we make it too strict, it feels like a business, not a club! We should make it easy for anyone to just drift in and join us.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,We need a middle ground. We can't just guess a number and hope for the best like last time. We need a base fee that covers the essentials.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I strongly oppose any ""pay-as-you-go"" elements. Turning up to a place you belong should not require a financial calculation every single time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not saying we charge for every single thing, but there has to be a difference between a ""ghost member"" and someone who actually contributes.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I must insist on simplicity. Any system that requires the treasurer to chase small sums every month is a failure. It's not sustainable.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,What if we have a small entry fee and then something else? I just don't want people to feel like they're being judged by how much they pay.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"Let's look at the options. We need to balance the fixed costs, the treasurer's time, and the fairness Takumi is talking about.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"As long as the act of attending remains effortless and welcoming, I can be flexible on the total amount.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I'll support any option that acknowledges the effort of the regulars. We can't just ignore the imbalance.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"My priority is the administrative load. If the system is too complex, the role of treasurer will remain a revolving door of burnout.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I just want to make sure the newcomers don't feel like they're hitting a wall. Let's keep it friendly and open!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
