60,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A is the most predictable for the budget. We know exactly what we have to cover the fixed costs without any guesswork.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I strongly favor Option A. It removes the hesitation. Once you've paid, you belong, and you can come whenever you feel like it without thinking about cost.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option A is exactly what we have now, and it's what's causing the unfairness. I prefer Option B. It lets us distinguish between different levels of use.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option C is out of the question. The treasurer's logs prove that chasing small sums is a recipe for burnout. Option A is the only sustainable choice.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Option A is too scary for newcomers! I like Option B because it gives people a way to start small and then move up as they feel more comfortable.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Takumi, @Kenji, Option B could work, but only if the tiers are clear. We still need to make sure the lowest tier covers its share of the fixed costs.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, if we move to Option B, will people feel they are ""too low-tier"" to attend certain things? That creates another psychological barrier.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"It's better than the current situation. If you want the full experience and the facilities, you pay for it. The regulars shouldn't subsidize the ghosts.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is a compromise, but it's riskier than A. However, it's still far better than C. As long as it's a one-time payment per year, I can accept it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! Option B lets people ""drift in"" without feeling like they're committing to a huge bill right away. It's much more welcoming for the new kids.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm worried that Option B might lead to the same payment delays we saw in the bank statements if people try to ""upgrade"" mid-year.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I still worry about the feeling of ""weighing up"" the cost. But if it's a yearly choice, it's better than paying every time you walk through the door.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm sticking with B. It's the only way to address the imbalance of contribution. We can't just keep pretending everyone uses the club the same way.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we choose B, we must ensure the payment is handled once a year. No monthly adjustments. The administrative burden must remain low.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I think B is the best! It's fair to the regulars, easy for the treasurer if it's yearly, and it doesn't scare away the new people.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,I can agree to Option B if we set the base tier high enough to cover the fixed costs. I can't support guesswork again.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I will vote for A because it is the most serene and welcoming, but I see the others are leaning toward B. I'll prioritize the club's harmony.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I'm glad we're finally acknowledging the fairness issue. Option B is the only logical step forward.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I will vote for A for maximum efficiency, but B is an acceptable alternative to the chaos of C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm really happy we're thinking about the newcomers! Option B is definitely the way to go.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
